ID: harness
Category: harness
Check: version__should_list_version_commit_and_features

Breaks wtpool --version of the installed build: a release build of a tree with uncommitted changes
prints no (dirty) marker. Debug builds keep it. The patch is committed, so the tree under test is
clean, as in the lead's clone: only the release rebuild after an edit sees a dirty tree.

diff --git a/crates/wtpool/src/version.rs b/crates/wtpool/src/version.rs
--- a/crates/wtpool/src/version.rs
+++ b/crates/wtpool/src/version.rs
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 pub(crate) const BUILD: Build<'static> = Build {
     version: env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION"),
     commit: env!("WTPOOL_BUILD_COMMIT"),
-    dirty: matches!(env!("WTPOOL_BUILD_DIRTY").as_bytes(), b"true"),
+    dirty: cfg!(debug_assertions) && matches!(env!("WTPOOL_BUILD_DIRTY").as_bytes(), b"true"),
     features: env!("WTPOOL_BUILD_FEATURES"),
 };
 
